  },
  {
    "episode_id": 72838,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72838.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Well, absolutely. It is the direct result of a worsening economy. I mean, clearly, I mean, no one. Do you think that that I would want for people to be on food stamps. I would hope that people wouldn't be, because that would say to me that the economy was growing, that people are working, people are more comfortable. We want to get to a point where the allocations for food stamps are reduced significantly, but this is not the time at which to do it.",
