        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker acknowledges a personal commitment to solving youth obesity within one generation.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Hunger and obesity are complex societal issues that cannot be easily resolved.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Obesity among young people is linked to financial hardship.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The coexistence of hunger and obesity indicates systemic failures in food access and distribution.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Society should prioritize addressing health disparities like youth obesity.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Financial deprivation directly contributes to poor dietary choices leading to obesity.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "A generational solution to obesity is both feasible and ethically necessary.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker views the link between poverty and obesity as counterintuitive or paradoxical.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Correction / Challenge"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 72838,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72838.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "You are correct and I have to as well have this same discussion with my colleagues because they would make the same argument to me. But if they look at the many of the issues that surround obesity and I will just just count some of them off for you. Most poor people live in environments where they can't even access healthy food. If you have a grocery store that is two miles from you",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
