    "turn_text": "I do. Now, let me just say this. Now, there are some things about the nutrition guidelines that I don't like myself, and I know young people are not going to like it, because when you think about the fact that Most young people, especially in urban areas, it is unusual for them to have a salad for lunch. But there are some other things that we have to think about and take into consideration some of the cultural differences that we experience. But I would say that farmers in particular need to be as supportive of these programs as possible because here, even in an urban area like mine, we participate in Know Your Farm and Know Your Food. We participate in local food banks. We participate in a lot of things that help farmers as well as help So we need to find a way to get fresh fruits and vegetables into our schools and into our food banks. And so, yeah, I do support the guidelines. They're not perfect. And we do probably need to make some adjustments as we go forward, but they're a good start.",
